// Screen-space width
//
// How much one pixel of screen travel changes a value — the graph-facing
// spelling of `fwidth`. The caller-side recipe an anti-aliased width
// wants: feed a distance field's `screen_width` into `sdf_coverage`'s
// `width`, and the coverage ramp is always about one pixel wide however
// the surface foreshortens. A constant width aliases exactly where the
// field crosses texel boundaries steeply.
//
// Fragment-only by construction: the derivative *is* the measurement.
// The stage analysis refuses a graph that feeds the vertex stage with
// this node (ADR 0054).
fn screen_width(
    value: f32, // The quantity whose pixel-to-pixel change matters. @default 0.0
) -> f32 {
    return fwidth(value);
}
